00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:17,650
Joestar?

266
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:21,257
Now prepare to be blown away!

267
00:18:21,340 --> 00:18:23,100
Tum-ta-da-da!

268
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:25,660
Here he is!

269
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:30,640
That sly bastard Avdol is
still alive, isn't that great?

270
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:36,039
Well, we should probably get going.

271
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:39,386
Here, allow me to help
you carry your luggage.

272
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:41,257
Avdol, how you been doing?

273
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:42,257
It's been a while.

274
00:18:42,340 --> 00:18:43,170
How goes it?

275
00:18:43,253 --> 00:18:46,017
So, Avdol, is the wound on
your back healing up all right?

276
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:49,257
It's fine, though my joints do
get a little stiff sometimes.

277
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:50,170
Hey!

278
00:18:50,253 --> 00:18:52,717
Has it really been two weeks
since we last saw each other?

279
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:53,630
Hey!

280
00:18:53,713 --> 00:18:54,857
We're lucky to all be alive.

281
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:57,237
Jotaro, you're still wearing your uniform?

282
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:58,673
Don't you ever get hot?

283
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:01,740
Hey, just hold on a second, guys.

284
00:19:04,140 --> 00:19:05,177
Didn't you hear me?

285
00:19:05,260 --> 00:19:07,737
I told you to hold on
a second, you assholes.

286
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:10,257
What's the deal with those
laissez-faire attitudes?

287
00:19:10,340 --> 00:19:13,057
A man we thought was dead
just waltzed onto the beach.

288
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:16,657
How the hell can you just brush it
off and act like nothing has changed?

289
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:19,211
Oh, yeah, I'm sorry about that, Polnareff.

290
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:24,740
When I told you I'd taken it upon myself
to bury Avdol in India, I may have lied.

291
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:29,000
What the hell?! Mr.

292
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:31,817
Joestar and Jotaro were the
ones who tended to the wounds

293
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:35,194
on my head back in India after
I was shot by Hull Horse.

294
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:40,817
You assholes have known Avdol was
alive the entire time and never

295
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:43,917
once stood across any of your
deceitful minds to let me know!

296
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,997
I'm most surprised at you, Kakyoin!

297
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:48,257
I only found out the day
after it all happened,

298
00:19:48,340 --> 00:19:50,857
But it was imperative to
not let the enemy know,

299
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:52,557
and since you have such a big mouth,

300
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:54,080
I suggested... Pardon.

301
00:19:54,420 --> 00:19:57,457
What I meant to say was, since it's
not easy for you to lie on command,

302
00:19:57,540 --> 00:19:59,952
I suggested we keep it a secret from you.

303
00:20:01,980 --> 00:20:06,137
If you'd let the secret slip, Avdol wouldn't
have been able to recuperate in peace.

304
00:20:06,220 --> 00:20:09,657
We were planning to let you know the
very moment we knew that he was safe.

305
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:12,177
But we didn't think
you'd run into him first.

306
00:20:12,260 --> 00:20:13,090
Oh, yeah!

307
00:20:13,173 --> 00:20:16,337
Avdol, we found your dad
living in a hut on this island!

308
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:17,857
Come on, let's let him know you're here!

309
00:20:17,940 --> 00:20:20,240
Oh, that was just me in disguise.

310
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:23,230
Say what?

311
00:20:24,580 --> 00:20:27,077
Then you were in on it
from the very start?

312
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:29,617
Everything that happened
was a ruse you created?

313
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:30,720
Don't talk to me!

314
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:34,257
No one ever comes to visit when
they have good news to report!

315
00:20:34,340 --> 00:20:35,480
Just shut up!

316
00:20:36,740 --> 00:20:37,660
Don't go there.

317
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:39,717
Avdol's death wasn't your fault.

318
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:41,624
You didn't have to go that far!

319
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:43,657
How dare you leave me out of the loop!

320
00:20:43,740 --> 00:20:46,417
I think that's the cruelest
thing you've ever done to me!

321
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:47,680
Now, now, chin up.

322
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:49,457
There's no reason for you to cry.

323
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:50,757
I'm sorry, Polnareff.

324
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:53,193
I truly didn't think you'd be this hurt.

325
00:20:54,140 --> 00:20:55,780
I apologize as well,

326
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:59,577
but I had a very good reason for
coming to this island in disguise.

327
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:00,637
Yeah, what is it?

328
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:03,097
It was partially so the
enemy wouldn't find out.

329
00:21:03,180 --> 00:21:07,117
But I also had Abdal do some shopping
for me while he was laying low.

330
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,500
What kind of shopping?

331
00:21:08,820 --> 00:21:11,397
Since it was a very
conspicuous acquisition,

332
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:14,460
I disguised myself as a
wealthy Arab gentleman.

333
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:16,320
All right, everyone.

334
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:18,642
Let's climb aboard and head out.

335
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:20,060
Come on, Polnareff.

336
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:22,997
